.claude/plans/PLAN-178/staged-loteB/codex_loteB_r30.md:12:  In `ADR-191-spawn-acceptance-contract-v2.md:54-55`, the advisory window is defined as counting every `path_count=0` event as a would-block, but explicit `NONE-READ-ONLY` declarations are valid and also emit `path_count=0`; they are the generator's default when `--files` is omitted. Counting only this field therefore labels compliant read-only spawns as rejected inputs and makes the calibration unusable; the query must exclude the dedicated read-only `path_hashes` marker.
