   252	## [1.2.0] - 2026-07-30
   253	
   254	Substrate + rail release (PLAN-160/161/163/164). The headline is not a new
   255	feature: it is that the cross-model pair-rail **completed a live in-hook
   256	review for the first time in the audit log's history**. Everything else is
   257	the substrate work that made that possible. As always: governance and
   258	auditability — no speed claim.
   259	
   260	### Fixed — the pair-rail was 100% fail-open (PLAN-164, ADR-110-AMEND-1)
   261	
   262	- **`CEO_PAIR_RAIL_TIMEOUT_S` internal default 30 → 120 s**, and the
   263	  `check_pair_rail.py` PreToolUse **registration timeout 60 → 150 s** in both
   264	  kernel `.claude/settings.json` and `templates/settings/settings.base.json`
   265	  (parity enforced). The 30 s value was an implementation literal, never a
   266	  decided one, and it sat structurally *below* the latency of a real Codex
   267	  verdict: **every one of the 12 `pair_rail_case` events in the entire life of
   268	  the audit log was case F / TIMEOUT.** The rail had never once completed a
   269	  live review. Measured calibration (N=9, same machine): p95 ≈ 75 s, which
   270	  crosses the measurement protocol's own 70 s escalation threshold and selects
   271	  120/150 rather than the 100/120 first draft.
   272	- **The layering invariant is now tested, not assumed**
   273	  (`test_pair_rail_timeout_invariant.py`): kernel registration == template
   274	  registration, and `registration >= internal + 30`. A unilateral flip of any
   275	  of the three literals now goes red in the suite and in the pack preflight.
